PRODUCT MANAGEMENT: IDEATION - SCAMPER & BLUE OCEAN
====================================================

1. WHAT IS IDEATION?
--------------------
Ideation means generating ideas for new products or finding ways to improve
existing products.

Suppose you have created a text-to-audio product like TTA. You want to make it
more useful for people who create videos. You might ask:
- How can I make it easier to use?
- What features are missing?
- How can I make it different from other AI voice tools?
- Why would someone choose my product instead of a competitor's?

Product managers use frameworks such as SCAMPER and Blue Ocean Strategy to
answer these questions.


2. SCAMPER: SEVEN WAYS TO IMPROVE A PRODUCT
-------------------------------------------
SCAMPER is a creative thinking framework. Each letter represents a different
way to generate ideas.

S - SUBSTITUTE (Replace something)
    Ask: What can I replace with something better?
    AI example: Replace expensive, paid text-to-speech APIs with a reliable,
    lower-cost alternative, while maintaining good voice quality.

C - COMBINE (Join two things)
    Ask: What two features could work better together?
    AI example: Combine text-to-speech with automatic subtitles, so video
    creators can generate narration and captions in one place.

A - ADAPT (Borrow an idea from somewhere else)
    Ask: What works in another product that I can adapt?
    AI example: Adapt the document templates used in presentation tools to
    create ready-made narration templates for YouTube videos, tutorials and
    advertisements.

M - MODIFY (Change or improve something)
    Ask: What can I make faster, simpler, or more useful?
    AI example: Add controls for speaking speed, pauses, pronunciation and
    voice style.

P - PUT TO ANOTHER USE (Find a new use)
    Ask: Who else could benefit from this technology?
    AI example: Use text-to-speech not just for YouTube creators, but also for
    teachers making lessons, students creating revision audio, or businesses
    producing training materials.

E - ELIMINATE (Remove something unnecessary)
    Ask: What makes the product complicated or frustrating?
    AI example: Remove unnecessary setup steps. Let users paste text, select a
    voice and generate audio without navigating several pages.

R - REVERSE (Change the usual order or approach)
    Ask: What if I did things in the opposite order?
    AI example: Instead of making users write a complete script before
    generating audio, let them describe their video idea first and have AI
    create a draft script and narration.

Remember: SCAMPER doesn't automatically give you a successful product idea. It
helps you generate ideas that you can later test with real users.


3. BLUE OCEAN STRATEGY: CREATE A DIFFERENT KIND OF PRODUCT
----------------------------------------------------------
Imagine there are 100 AI text-to-speech tools in the market. Most compete on
the same things:
- Voice quality
- Number of voices
- Pricing
- Generation speed

RED OCEAN
Many competitors fighting for the same customers.
- Same audience
- Similar features
- Price competition

BLUE OCEAN
A market space where you create a different kind of value, reducing direct
competition.
- Underserved audience
- Different experience
- New source of value

Example: Building a better AI audio product

Suppose you discover that many beginner video creators struggle to produce
narration, subtitles and a ready-to-use script.

Instead of building just another text-to-speech tool, you create an AI Video
Narration Workspace. It helps users:
1. Turn an idea into a script.
2. Generate voice narration.
3. Create subtitles.
4. Organize audio and captions for editing.

The product is now solving a broader workflow problem, not just converting
text into speech.

This is a potential Blue Ocean opportunity, not proof that no competitors
exist. You would still research the market and validate whether customers
actually want it.

Four useful Blue Ocean questions (the ERRC Grid)

  ELIMINATE - What can you remove?
              Example: Complicated setup
  REDUCE    - What can you make less burdensome?
              Example: Manual editing steps
  RAISE     - What can you improve significantly?
              Example: Ease of use
  CREATE    - What new value can you introduce?
              Example: Script-to-narration workflow


4. HOW SCAMPER AND BLUE OCEAN WORK TOGETHER
-------------------------------------------
Step 1: SCAMPER
        Generate many possible improvements and new ideas.

Step 2: BLUE OCEAN THINKING
        Identify ideas that could deliver different value to an underserved
        audience.

Step 3: VALIDATE
        Talk to potential customers, study competitors and test a simple
        prototype.
